  "answer": "This feature request has been made before. The main tracking issue is PowerToys#46333 (Privacy Overlay). It proposes a hotkey, similar to Always on Top, that excludes a chosen window from screen sharing, recording and screenshots. PowerToys#48566 was closed as a duplicate of it. PowerToys#34950 asks for the same thing (window masking via WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE) and was closed as a duplicate of #13035. A commenter on that ticket disputed that duplicate link. The feature is not available yet. Subscribe to and upvote #46333 and add your use case there. A contributor has built a proof of concept, and it showed that calling SetWindowDisplayAffinity directly from another process is blocked even when elevated. Their version works by injecting a hook DLL into the target app. For now, the open-source tools winhider and Invisiwind (linked in #34950) do something similar. They don't detect newly opened windows."
 },
